cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use EvoJump, please cite it as below."
title: "EvoJump: A Comprehensive Framework for Evolutionary Ontogenetic Analysis"
authors:
  - family-names: Friedman
    given-names: Daniel Ari
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6232-9096"
    affiliation: "Active Inference Institute"
version: 0.5.2
date-released: "2026-09-08"
license: Apache-2.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22664675
repository-code: "https://github.com/docxology/EvoJump"
abstract: "EvoJump models ontogenetic development as a jump-diffusion process sweeping across a fixed analytical plane, yielding dynamic cross-sectional views of phenotypic distributions across a developmental timeline. Includes data QC, seven stochastic process models, cross-sectional distribution analysis, visualization/animation, evolutionary sampling, and a statistical analysis engine."
keywords:
  - evo-devo
  - ontogeny
  - jump-diffusion
  - stochastic processes
  - quantitative genetics
